{"id": "186675", "name": "נגזרות חלקיות קיימות ורציפות? – x²·cos(1/(x+y))", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<p dir=\"rtl\" style=\"text-align: right;\"></p>\n<p dir=\"rtl\" style=\"text-align: right;\"></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: right; direction: rtl;\" dir=\"rtl\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">נגדיר פונקציה \\(f(x,y)&nbsp; \\) באופן הבא:&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">\\( f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{array}{cc}{{CT:0}} &amp; (x,y)\\neq (0,0) \\\\0 &amp; (x,y)=(0,0)\\end{array}\\right. \\)</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: right;\" dir=\"rtl\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">הגרף של \\(f(x,y)\\) נראה כך.</span></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left; direction: ltr;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><img style=\"display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" src=\"data/186675/files/1.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"469\" height=\"459\"></span></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: right;\" dir=\"rtl\"><strong style=\"font-size: medium;\">מצאו את הנגזרות החלקיות של \\(f(x,y)\\) ואת ערכן בנקודה \\((0,0)\\):&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<p></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: right;\" dir=\"rtl\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">(כדי להקליד אינסוף, הקלידו&nbsp;<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">inf</span>, ועל מנת להקליד מינוס אינסוף, הקלידו&nbsp;<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">minf.</span>&nbsp;אם הנגזרת לא קיימת הקלידו&nbsp;<span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">nd</span>)</span></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: right;\" dir=\"rtl\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">שימו לב</span>: תשובתכן תוצג כפי שהמערכת מבינה אותה. אנא וודעו שהיא נראית כמצופה.&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: right;\" dir=\"rtl\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\"><br>\n    </span></p>\n<table align=\"center\">\n    <tbody>\n        <tr>\n            <td>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\)=</td>\n            <td>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\)=</td>\n            <td>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((0,0)\\)=</td>\n            <td>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n            <td>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((0,0)\\)=</td>\n            <td>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</td>\n        </tr>\n    </tbody>\n</table>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">האם \\(f(x,y)\\) רציפה ב- <strong>\\((0,0)\\)</strong>? [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</span></p>\n<p style=\"direction: rtl; text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: medium;\">האם לכל פונקציה רציפה בהכרח יש נגזרות חלקיות? [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]]</span></p>\n<p></p>\n<p></p>", "generalfeedback": "", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br>[[feedback:prt2]]<br>[[feedback:prt3]]<br>[[feedback:prt4]]<br>[[feedback:prt5]]<br>[[feedback:prt6]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 25, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans4", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans5", "type": "boolean", "boxsize": 10, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 2, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans6", "type": "boolean", "boxsize": 15, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "an1:ans1;\nif listp(ans1) then an1:ans1[1];", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "an1", "tans": "fx", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is incorrect.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "an2:ans2;\nif listp(ans2) then an2:ans2[1];", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "an2", "tans": "fy", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<p>\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((x,y)\\) is incorrect.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Correct answer,&nbsp;\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\((0,0)=0\\)</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt3-1-F", "feedback": "<p>Inorrect answer. By definition</p>\n<p>&nbsp;\\( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\)\\( (0,0)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(h,0)-f(0,0)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{h^2 \\cdot cos(\\frac{1}{h})}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}h \\cdot cos(\\frac{1}{h})=0 \\)</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt4", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans4", "tans": "0", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt4-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Correct answer,&nbsp;\\(\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\((0,0)=0\\)</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt4-1-F", "feedback": "<p>Inorrect answer. By definition \\( \\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\)\\( (0,0)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f(0,h)-f(0,0)}{h}=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{0 \\cdot cos(\\frac{1}{h})}{h}=0 \\)</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt5", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans5", "tans": "true", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt5-1-T", "feedback": "<p>Continuity of \\(f(x,y)\\). Well done! Indeed \\(f(x,y)\\) is continuous.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>For all \\((x,y)\\neq(0,0) \\), \\(f(x,y)\\) is an elementary function and hence continuous. As for \\((x,y)=(0,0) \\) we can easily calculate the limit using the sandwich lemma, noting that \\(|f(x,y)| \\le x^2\\), so that \\( \\lim_{(x,y) \\to (0,0)} x^2 \\cdot cos(\\frac{1}{x+y})= \\lim_{(x,y)\\to (0,0)} x^2 =0=f(0,0) \\). Therefore \\(f(x,y)\\) is also continuous at \\((0,0)\\).</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt5-1-F", "feedback": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Inorrect answer,&nbsp;\\(f(x,y)\\) is continuous.For all \\((x,y)\\neq(0,0) \\), \\(f(x,y)\\) is an elementary function. As for \\((0,0)\\) try showing continuity using the sandwich lemma.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt6", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans6", "tans": "false", "testoptions": null, "quiet": true, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt6-1-T", "feedback": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Does a continuous function always have partial derivatives. Your answer is correct! Our function here does have partial derivatives. But this is not always the case. In fact, just a few questions ago we saw a counterexample. The function \\(g(x,y)=x \\sin(\\frac{20}{x+y})\\) when \\((x,y) \\ne (0,0)\\) and \\(g(0,0)=0\\) is an example. See if you can find more such examples.&nbsp;</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt6-1-F", "feedback": "<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Does a continuous function always have partial derivatives. Your answer is incorrect! Our function here is continuous and it does have partial derivatives. But don't let this confuse you, some continuous functions do not have partial derivatives. See if you can find a counterexample.&nbsp;</p>"}}]}], "qvnames": ["f", "fx", "fy"], "nvariants": 1}